<title>USA: Carter-Wallace Q3 shr $0.23 vs $0.22.</title>
<headline>Carter-Wallace Q3 shr $0.23 vs $0.22.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>THREE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>					  Dec 31, 1996     Dec 31, 1995</p>
<p> Sales				  $163,020,000     $162,004,000</p>
<p> Earnings Before Taxes		17,821,000	 17,421,000</p>
<p> Income Taxes			    7,307,000	  7,143,000</p>
<p> Net Earnings			   10,514,000	 10,278,000</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share			    .23		  .22</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding	 46,396,000	 46,138,000</p>
<p>					   NINE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>					   Dec 31,1996	Dec 31,1995</p>
<p> Sales				  $492,441,000     $493,851,000</p>
<p>Earnings Before One-Time</p>
<p> Charges and Taxes		    43,009,000	 47,812,000</p>
<p> One-Time Charges				  -  (36,600,000)(a)</p>
<p> Earnings Before Taxes		43,009,000	 11,212,000</p>
<p> Income Taxes			   17,634,000	  4,597,000</p>
<p> Net Earnings			   25,375,000	  6,615,000</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share			    .55		  .14</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding	 46,392,000	 46,136,000</p>
<p>Note: (a) In the prior year, the Company incurred one-time charges related to the closure of its condom manufacturing plant in Trenton, New Jersey and the restructuring of operations and facilities.</p>
<p>These one-time costs resulted in a pre-tax charge of $36,600,000 ($21,600,000 after tax or $0.47 per share) for the nine months ended December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
